Step 5: Automatic Long-Term Memory

Instead, we'll start with a simple pattern:

Conversation
     ↓
Ask LLM:
"Did the user provide any
new persistent information?"
     ↓
Extract structured facts
     ↓
Python validates result
     ↓
Update user_memory.json

This introduces a very important Agentic AI concept:

The LLM proposes an action/data change; Python controls whether that change actually happens.

The LLM doesn't directly get permission to modify your filesystem.



The important principle is:

The LLM proposes memory. Python decides whether that memory is acceptable.

